      en: "Pottinger Peak is a 406-meter mountain on Hong Kong Island, named after Sir Henry Pottinger, the first Governor of Hong Kong. Located in Aberdeen Country Park, it overlooks Deep Water Bay. The Pottinger Peak Trail is a moderate hike through secondary forest. The summit is a popular launch site for paragliding due to consistent winds. It is part of the Hong Kong Trail, offering a blend of nature and history.",
